---
// src/components/Faq.astro
---

<section class="mt-14 pt-8 border-t border-white/[0.08] space-y-3">
  <div class="text-[11px] font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-zinc-500 mb-4 text-center">
    Frequently Asked Questions
  </div>

  <details class="group bg-zinc-900/40 border border-white/[0.06] rounded-xl p-4 transition-colors hover:border-white/15">
    <summary class="text-xs font-medium text-zinc-200 cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
      <span>Why is trimming instant and lossless?</span>
      <span class="text-zinc-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform font-mono text-xs">↓</span>
    </summary>
    <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 mt-2.5 leading-relaxed pt-2 border-t border-white/[0.04]">
      Conventional video cutters re-encode the entire video stream, creating compression artifacts and taking minutes. YT—CUT performs a direct stream demux/mux (<code class="font-mono text-zinc-300">-c copy</code>) in WebAssembly. Frames and audio packets are transferred bit-for-bit in seconds.
    </p>
  </details>

  <details class="group bg-zinc-900/40 border border-white/[0.06] rounded-xl p-4 transition-colors hover:border-white/15">
    <summary class="text-xs font-medium text-zinc-200 cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
      <span>What is the maximum allowed clip duration?</span>
      <span class="text-zinc-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform font-mono text-xs">↓</span>
    </summary>
    <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 mt-2.5 leading-relaxed pt-2 border-t border-white/[0.04]">
      You can trim clips up to 10 minutes (600 seconds) from videos of any length (even multi-hour podcasts or livestreams). The 10-minute window protects browser memory while covering virtually all highlight, clip, and quote requirements.
    </p>
  </details>

  <details class="group bg-zinc-900/40 border border-white/[0.06] rounded-xl p-4 transition-colors hover:border-white/15">
    <summary class="text-xs font-medium text-zinc-200 cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
      <span>Are any video bytes stored on your servers?</span>
      <span class="text-zinc-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform font-mono text-xs">↓</span>
    </summary>
    <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 mt-2.5 leading-relaxed pt-2 border-t border-white/[0.04]">
      Never. Our Cloudflare Worker acts only as a stateless pass-through for stream metadata and range chunking. Video data is piped directly into your browser's private memory and saved straight to your device.
    </p>
  </details>
</section>
